WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
Bitcoin will continue to grow as digital capital.

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.480
It'll serve as a long-term store of value for the world.

3
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.220
Right now, it's 0.1% of the world's assets.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.900
It's about $1.4 trillion out of $900 trillion.

5
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.460
It's big in crypto economy, but it's fairly small in mainstream economy.

6
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.580
I think the entire worldwide addressable market for store of value

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.920
for long-term capital is about $450 trillion.

8
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.860
So 1.4 out of $450 trillion.

9
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.960
And I expect Bitcoin will grow progressively

10
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.780
to be 7% of the assets of the world, not 0.1%.

11
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.380
And when it gets to 7%, it'll be $13 million a coin.

12
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.120
So $13 million, and that's over 21 years.

13
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.800
So by the year 2045.

14
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.320
And I think right now, it's been growing.

15
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.120
For the last four years, it's been up about 50% a year.

16
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.180
And it's gradually decelerating its growth rate

17
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:10.240
because as it gets bigger and as it gets more widely adopted

18
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.780
and the law of large numbers kicks in, it should decelerate.

19
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.680
If you look back over the last 100 years,

20
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.400
the US dollar money supply expands about 7% a year.

21
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.080
So I'm just thinking it'll continue for the next 20 or 30 years at that trend.

22
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:33.500
And once you crank in that number and some assumptions about inflation and technology,

23
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:40.380
the conclusion is all the other asset classes will grow plus or minus a few percent.

24
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.520
Equity will grow a bit faster.

25
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.580
Real estate about the same, perhaps gold slower.

26
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:54.280
Bitcoin will grow faster because it is demonetizing gold, demonetizing real estate,

27
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:00.920
demonetizing certain equity indexes, and demonetizing corporate bond portfolios.

28
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:06.620
These are all things that wealthy people store their wealth in, in order to just keep it.

29
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:16.220
And so if you see Bitcoin is going 50% to 45% growth to 40% growth to 35% growth to 32% growth

30
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:24.560
to 30% to 28% to 25%, at some point, it's approaching the returns of the S&P index or equity indexes.

31
00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.560
And they've been like 12%, you know, 10% to 12%.

32
00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.420
And so Bitcoin is moving toward that.

33
00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.500
Those companies are going to buy Bitcoin.

34
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.580
And as they buy Bitcoin, they're going to actually merge.

35
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.580
And so these two lines of what we'll call traditional capital,

36
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:46.320
which is diversified equity portfolios, and digital capital, which is what Bitcoin is,

37
00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.440
they're moving toward each other.

38
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:54.400
The volatility of conventional corporations is the VIX.

39
00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.080
If you study the VIX, and it's like 15, 16.

40
00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.760
And the volatility of Bitcoin is what we call devol.

41
00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.280
And you can, it's like 55.

42
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.620
The devol is moving toward the VIX.

43
00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:14.700
And when Bitcoin is a $200 trillion asset class, you know, maybe the Bitcoin volatility is 20.

44
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.480
And the VIX is 15.

45
00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.560
Bitcoin's always going to be a bit more volatile.

46
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.960
It's always going to be performing a bit more.

47
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:28.260
Because it's global, open 24-7, pure digital capital.

48
00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.760
And it strips away the risk factors of companies, corporations.

49
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.860
And it strips away the risk factors of property, right?

50
00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.540
Of real estate.

51
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.020
And so that's why it's going to outperform.

52
00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:46.000
And I've explained why it's more volatile, because it's always going to be more tradable, more global.

53
00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.880
Some guy can short it with 100x leverage in Singapore at midnight.

54
00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.820
That's illegal in New York to do with equity.

55
00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:58.940
So the point is, there are some things you can do with Bitcoin you'll never do with traditional assets.

56
00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:05.620
But when you crank all that in, and I did it in a model, it's called the Bitcoin 24 model.

57
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.500
You can Google Bitcoin 24.

58
00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.640
And if you Google it, you'll find a link to GitHub.

59
00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.560
And you can go download the Bitcoin 24 model.

60
00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.880
And you can put in all your own assumptions for all these macroeconomic factors and all these technical factors.

61
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:25.160
And you can run your own micro models for your family and your corporation and your country.

62
00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.800
So, you know, don't take my word for it.

63
00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:28.520
Try it out yourself.

64
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:37.080
But if you download Bitcoin 24 or you look at my assumptions, my assumptions are basically, you know, those things.

65
00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:43.880
And the result that pops out is Bitcoin, you know, on average over the 21 years has an annualized rate of return of 29%.

66
00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:52.060
And that 29% just, it grows with volatility up to 13 million of Bitcoin.

67
00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:59.820
So you can, if you wanted to figure out how much will you have in 10 years, you could download the model and put in your assumptions and look at the 10-year point.

68
00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.620
Maybe you're more bearish.

69
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.120
The bear case would be only 3 million a coin.

70
00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.640
And the bull case is 49 million a coin.

71
00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.580
Everyone can have their own assumptions.

72
00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:21.700
But, you know, I think if you want something simple, if you want to reduce to a simple sentence, I would say if you're a young person, every Bitcoin you buy today is probably worth $13 million in U.S. dollars in 21 years.

73
00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:25.300
So if you can get 5 Bitcoin, you would have 65 million.

74
00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:31.540
Now, it won't buy as much in 21 years as it buys today, but it'll buy a lot.

75
00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.460
It'll buy, you know, it'll buy a lot.

76
00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:41.880
I mean, consumer products will appreciate it 2% or 3% a year or they'll get cheaper because of technology.

77
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:55.600
And on the other hand, Palm Beach real estate, if you want a beach house in the Hamptons or Palm Beach or you want the best condo in the middle of the biggest city, that's going to go up 7%, you know, 6%, 7%.

78
00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:03.000
So, you know, you kind of, you want to beat the 7% if you want to buy rich things, expensive things.

79
00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.320
You want to beat the 2% if you want to buy the cheap things.

80
00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.920
And I think Bitcoin kind of beats everything.

81
00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.880
So that's why it's a pretty good idea.
